---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base";
import { Icon } from "astro-icon";

const meta = {
	title: "The Whale Coffee",
	description:
		"A specialty coffee brand I ran in 2020 and 2021, sold on Amazon UK. It led directly to Coffee Galley.",
};
---

<PageLayout meta={meta}>
	<div class="max-w-2xl">
		<div class="mb-8 flex items-center gap-4">
			<img src="/whaleCoffeeIcon.png" alt="The Whale Coffee logo" class="h-20 w-20 rounded-2xl" />
			<div>
				<h1 class="title mb-1 text-3xl">The Whale Coffee</h1>
				<p class="text-gray-500">2020-2021</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<section class="mb-8">
			<p class="mb-4">
				A specialty coffee brand. I designed the label, sourced the beans from a roaster, and sold
				the bags on Amazon UK. Instagram did the marketing.
			</p>
			<p class="mb-4">
				The interesting part was not the coffee. It was realising how much of running a coffee
				brand is plumbing: roaster communication, packaging, labels, fulfilment. Every merchant
				repeats the same work. That observation became
				<a href="/apps/coffee-galley" class="project-link">Coffee Galley</a>, a Shopify app that
				did the plumbing for them.
			</p>
		</section>

		<div class="mb-12 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
			<a
				href="https://www.instagram.com/thewhalecoffee_/"
				target="_blank"
				rel="noopener noreferrer"
				class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md bg-accent px-4 py-2 text-bgColor transition-all hover:opacity-80"
			>
				<Icon name="fa-brands:instagram" class="h-5 w-5" />
				 Instagram
			</a>
		</div>
	</div>
</PageLayout>
